WEBVTT

00:03.860 --> 00:06.110
I'll be off, then.

00:06.510 --> 00:09.440
Please be careful on the way, Haruto.

00:09.440 --> 00:10.900
Off you go.

00:10.900 --> 00:13.020
We should be able to speak Strahl...

00:13.020 --> 00:16.120
...fluently by the time you come back.

00:16.540 --> 00:19.260
Aishia, I'm leaving everyone to you.

00:19.260 --> 00:20.390
You can count on me.

00:22.020 --> 00:23.600
Be careful now.

00:30.330 --> 00:31.430
Release Magic.

00:37.200 --> 00:38.270
Teleport.

00:40.290 --> 00:41.190
He's gone?!

00:41.190 --> 00:42.230
For real?!

00:42.230 --> 00:43.770
Whoa!

01:03.040 --> 01:05.570
SEIREI GENSOUKI - SPIRIT CHRONICLES SEASON 2

02:06.010 --> 02:07.020
Aki!

02:10.060 --> 02:13.020
Aishia, what was that?

02:13.020 --> 02:14.160
I think it's a monster.

02:15.990 --> 02:20.200
OUR HOME TARGETED

02:20.870 --> 02:23.050
The Spirit village...

02:23.050 --> 02:25.380
Looks like I could return here safely.

02:31.890 --> 02:33.510
Oh, it's you, Bro!

02:33.510 --> 02:34.730
Latifa!

02:35.180 --> 02:37.470
Welcome back, Bro!

02:38.630 --> 02:39.930
Welcome home!

02:40.320 --> 02:42.930
I'm back.
Have you been well?

02:42.930 --> 02:44.080
Yeah!

02:44.080 --> 02:46.440
I knew it! It's Rio!

02:47.370 --> 02:48.440
Rio...

02:48.440 --> 02:50.310
Welcome back.

02:50.310 --> 02:53.310
I felt a big magic distortion nearby,

02:53.310 --> 02:56.070
so I thought you might be back.

02:56.070 --> 02:59.770
Both Latifa and Sara
hurried to catch up with you.

02:59.770 --> 03:01.450
It was quite the commotion.

03:01.450 --> 03:06.820
You were trying
to get ahead of us too, Alma!

03:08.030 --> 03:11.180
You all just wanted to
see him soon, right?

03:16.240 --> 03:18.240
Actually, there's something...

03:18.240 --> 03:20.720
...I want to talk about with the elders.

03:21.150 --> 03:25.850
All right, I'll go tell them right away.

03:27.210 --> 03:30.160
So, the massive mana and od...

03:30.160 --> 03:32.860
...coming from Strahl...

03:32.860 --> 03:38.430
...is coming from the six light pillars,
that's what you're saying?

03:38.430 --> 03:39.870
Yes, perhaps.

03:41.380 --> 03:46.370
I think the light pillars are
some kind of space-time sorcery.

03:46.740 --> 03:51.380
It's like a summoning system
to invite people from another world.

03:52.000 --> 03:55.420
In Strahl, the Six Heroes who fought
in the Divine-Demon War...

03:55.420 --> 03:58.780
...have been rumoured to appear.

04:00.380 --> 04:01.680
The Heroes...

04:02.110 --> 04:03.150
Yes.

04:03.150 --> 04:10.320
Sir Rio, why do you think the Heroes
are from another world?

04:10.320 --> 04:11.190
The fact is...

04:11.750 --> 04:14.290
I'm sheltering two girls and one boy...

04:14.290 --> 04:17.320
...from another world in my place.

04:21.250 --> 04:24.100
So those three are the Heroes?

04:24.100 --> 04:27.670
No, I don't think they are.

04:27.670 --> 04:30.460
They were at a different
location from the pillars.

04:31.250 --> 04:34.210
However, there were two
other people in their group.

04:34.210 --> 04:35.900
And those three...

04:35.900 --> 04:39.090
...seemed to have witnessed the two
getting caught in the space distortion.

04:39.090 --> 04:42.650
So the ones summoned as Heroes...

04:42.650 --> 04:43.600
Yes.

04:43.600 --> 04:47.420
I think those three...

04:47.420 --> 04:50.100
...got involved in the summoning
of the other two.

04:51.710 --> 04:56.110
Sir Rio, you could communicate
with the otherworldly people?

04:56.110 --> 04:57.170
Yes.

04:57.920 --> 04:58.860
I could.

04:59.470 --> 05:03.840
To be precise, I knew their language.

05:03.840 --> 05:06.240
What do you mean?

05:06.240 --> 05:06.990
I...

05:07.630 --> 05:11.750
I once lived in the same world
as them in my previous life.

05:12.560 --> 05:13.750
Previous life?

05:14.560 --> 05:17.780
I'll talk about that
when I have the chance.

05:17.780 --> 05:22.230
Could you please accept
this reason for the time being?

05:25.430 --> 05:26.900
All right.

05:26.900 --> 05:29.270
Let's put this aside for now.

05:29.690 --> 05:31.010
Thank you.

05:31.390 --> 05:34.190
Also, it's a bit hard to ask,

05:34.620 --> 05:36.900
but I have a request.

05:37.360 --> 05:39.920
It's a request from no other than you.

05:39.920 --> 05:42.880
We'll do our best
to fulfill it when possible.

05:42.880 --> 05:45.070
About the three I mentioned...

05:45.070 --> 05:50.540
Can I ask for you to shelter them here,
alongside another one?

05:50.890 --> 05:53.540
Do you mind elaborating?

05:53.910 --> 05:56.250
I'm thinking of finding a way...

05:56.250 --> 06:00.170
...to get them back to their original world.

06:00.580 --> 06:05.180
However, I can't move around freely
while sheltering them.

06:05.530 --> 06:11.020
My expertise in space-time sorcery now
isn't comparable to the villagers here.

06:12.160 --> 06:16.710
When it comes to space-time sorcery
that allows moving across worlds,

06:16.710 --> 06:19.190
we also have no idea.

06:19.590 --> 06:24.130
So you want us to take care of them, correct?

06:24.130 --> 06:24.940
Yes.

06:25.310 --> 06:27.580
And who's the other one?

06:28.030 --> 06:30.310
My mentor.

06:30.310 --> 06:33.330
She was forced into
an unwanted political marriage.

06:33.330 --> 06:36.510
On the day of the wedding,
I saved her.

06:39.750 --> 06:42.870
I couldn't just turn a blind eye
on her predicament.

06:45.090 --> 06:48.500
Good going, you womaniser!

06:48.960 --> 06:52.260
Very well, we'll take care of them.

06:52.260 --> 06:53.100
Right?

06:53.570 --> 06:57.740
Good grief, you...
Well, I have no objections.

06:57.740 --> 06:59.120
Me either.

06:59.520 --> 07:00.110
However...

07:00.780 --> 07:04.370
When those four return to Strahl,

07:04.370 --> 07:09.140
I want you to make sure they're able
to keep this village's existence a secret.

07:09.140 --> 07:10.370
Of course.

07:10.370 --> 07:12.870
I'll explain to them myself.

07:13.520 --> 07:17.390
I'll depart tomorrow and bring them here.

07:19.070 --> 07:22.950
Latifa, do you understand
what we talked about earlier?

07:22.950 --> 07:24.020
Yeah.

07:25.410 --> 07:29.910
I spoke to you about
my previous life without permission.

07:29.910 --> 07:30.810
Sorry for that.

07:32.370 --> 07:34.050
But if I didn't do that,

07:34.490 --> 07:37.390
I wouldn't be able to explain
to the head elders.

07:38.690 --> 07:41.990
Should we have talked
about me back there?

07:42.370 --> 07:44.900
You don't have to.

07:44.900 --> 07:47.890
Those people...
They're Japanese, right?

07:48.250 --> 07:49.160
Yeah.

07:49.160 --> 07:52.910
So you also told them...

07:52.910 --> 07:55.730
...that you're also Japanese?

07:55.730 --> 08:00.330
If I didn't they'd be wondering
how I could understand their language.

08:02.950 --> 08:06.400
It was supposed to be our secret...

08:09.010 --> 08:12.190
Why are you laughing?!

08:12.190 --> 08:14.950
It's because you're cute, I guess.

08:16.080 --> 08:17.560
That's not fair...

08:18.390 --> 08:20.940
Not fair, Bro.

08:22.020 --> 08:23.260
Say, Latifa.

08:23.730 --> 08:27.130
Even where there's someone else
who knows Japan other than us,

08:27.130 --> 08:31.190
it won't change the fact
that you're still my special.

08:33.840 --> 08:36.320
Do you remember what I said
about my previous life?

08:36.800 --> 08:39.050
That I had a crush on my childhood friend,

08:39.050 --> 08:42.980
and I had a sister who was separated
by our parents' divorce.

08:45.230 --> 08:46.170
Yeah...

08:46.990 --> 08:49.510
One of the people I'm sheltering...

08:49.910 --> 08:53.680
...was the one I liked
as Haruto Amakawa...

08:54.050 --> 08:56.200
Her name is Miharu Ayase.

08:56.960 --> 08:57.680
Huh?

08:58.230 --> 08:59.580
And the other one...

09:00.250 --> 09:01.770
Aki Sendo.

09:01.770 --> 09:04.820
We were only together
for three years,

09:05.340 --> 09:07.020
but she was my little sister.

09:07.670 --> 09:08.940
Little sister...

09:09.630 --> 09:14.090
But I didn't tell them I have
the memories of Haruto Amakawa.

09:14.500 --> 09:15.720
Why?

09:16.210 --> 09:18.700
They're suddenly faced
with a strange world,

09:19.150 --> 09:21.850
and they must be mentally unstable.

09:22.580 --> 09:24.960
Besides, right now...

09:26.950 --> 09:28.630
I'm not Haruto Amakawa.

09:30.350 --> 09:35.120
So, you shouldn't talk about
my previous life to them.

09:36.780 --> 09:40.340
Don't you actually want to tell them?

09:40.340 --> 09:42.150
That's not true.

09:42.620 --> 09:45.930
Tell me how you truly feel!

09:46.300 --> 09:49.040
Or else I can't keep my promise...

09:49.590 --> 09:52.020
About who I am in the previous life...

09:52.990 --> 09:57.110
I'd like to make it
a secret just between us.

09:58.500 --> 10:01.500
Sure, I'll have to tell them someday,

10:02.290 --> 10:03.620
but not now.

10:05.300 --> 10:06.650
That's not fair...

10:07.570 --> 10:10.370
You really are unfair, Bro.

10:10.370 --> 10:12.880
I can't tell what you're feeling...

10:13.380 --> 10:14.580
...is a lie.

10:25.530 --> 10:28.160
How long will you be away?

10:28.660 --> 10:31.290
I think I can be back here
after about two months.

10:31.930 --> 10:34.300
I'll be off then, Latifa.

10:37.260 --> 10:38.370
Safe trip...

10:39.210 --> 10:40.370
Bro.

10:41.850 --> 10:44.460
She's still at the age
requiring some pampering, I guess.

10:46.580 --> 10:49.300
Don't worry about me, Latifa.

10:51.630 --> 10:53.730
I'll be on my way now.

10:55.310 --> 10:57.620
Have a safe trip!

11:04.270 --> 11:05.270
KINGDOM OF GALARC, ROYAL CAPITAL GALTUUK

11:05.270 --> 11:07.770
KINGDOM OF GALARC, ROYAL CAPITAL GALTUUK
That's all for the details of the happening

11:07.770 --> 11:09.400
in Beltrum's capital city.

11:09.910 --> 11:12.240
Thank you for the report.

11:12.240 --> 11:14.930
My pleasure, Your Majesty Francois.

11:14.930 --> 11:17.900
Sorry for asking this right
after you just returned,

11:17.900 --> 11:19.790
KING FRANCOIS GALARC
but I have a request for you.

11:19.790 --> 11:22.660
KING FRANCOIS GALARC
I'd like you to go to Duke Huguenot's place.

11:23.190 --> 11:24.450
Gladly.

11:24.820 --> 11:26.670
For what purpose?

11:27.090 --> 11:32.950
I'm sure you've heard of a hero coming
from the holy jewel we're possessing, right?

11:32.950 --> 11:34.180
Yes.

11:34.180 --> 11:37.680
She's a girl of the same age as me.

11:38.180 --> 11:41.440
Therefore, I would like to invite ambassadors
from neighbouring countries,

11:41.440 --> 11:45.050
and hold an evening party
to unveil our hero.

11:45.050 --> 11:46.190
I see.

11:46.640 --> 11:50.960
For that, I would also like
to invite Beltrum's hero...

11:50.960 --> 11:53.070
...to attend the party as well.

11:53.710 --> 11:58.110
Could you deliver the invitation on my behalf.

11:58.910 --> 12:01.080
I will see to it.

12:01.760 --> 12:05.620
I hear their hero is a young man.

12:05.620 --> 12:06.580
His name...

12:06.980 --> 12:09.360
...is Hiroaki Sakata.

12:09.360 --> 12:11.590
Master Hiroaki Sakata?

12:12.130 --> 12:12.880
Yeah.

12:13.230 --> 12:17.920
But he seems to be saying
his family name first.

12:17.920 --> 12:20.950
Sakata, Hiroaki...

12:21.350 --> 12:23.220
That name sounds nostalgic...

12:23.220 --> 12:26.980
Hm? What sounds nostalgic?

12:26.980 --> 12:31.250
Oh, I mean, it's quite an unfamiliar name.

12:31.250 --> 12:33.520
Hiroaki Sakata...

12:34.020 --> 12:35.360
Could that be...

12:37.010 --> 12:38.490
Um, Your Majesty?

12:38.910 --> 12:43.280
Could I ask what the name of our hero?

12:43.280 --> 12:45.490
Lady Sumeragi, first name Satsuki.

12:46.570 --> 12:49.740
Judging by how she introduced herself
with her family name first,

12:49.740 --> 12:52.410
she might be from
the same place as Sir Hiroaki.

12:52.410 --> 12:53.890
Same place...

12:53.890 --> 12:57.540
Hiroaki Sakata...
Satsuki Sumeragi.

12:57.540 --> 12:58.260
I knew it...

12:58.650 --> 13:03.270
I thought you should meet her,
so I had her waiting in another room.

13:03.270 --> 13:05.410
Charlotte, take her there.

13:05.410 --> 13:07.300
Okay, Father.

13:10.640 --> 13:13.770
Lady Satsuki, pardon the intrusion.

13:14.180 --> 13:14.950
Come in.

13:26.410 --> 13:27.730
Nice to meet you.

13:27.730 --> 13:30.140
Are you Miss Liselotte, by chance?

13:30.140 --> 13:31.000
SEIREI GENSOUKI - SPIRIT CHRONICLES SEASON 2

13:32.860 --> 13:36.000
Just what I'd expect from the city
chosen as Ricca Guild's headquarters.

13:36.850 --> 13:38.920
Quite the uniform excellence, eh?

13:41.340 --> 13:44.220
I've found myself some good substrates.

13:44.220 --> 13:45.510
Go forth.

13:46.060 --> 13:51.020
Find someone in the forest near Amande
enveloped in a large amount of mana,

13:51.020 --> 13:53.970
and bring them to me alive.

13:53.970 --> 13:58.000
Kill any unwanted witnesses
whenever able.

13:58.000 --> 14:01.530
You have until sundown tomorrow.

14:01.940 --> 14:05.690
More substrates will come
gathering by next time.

14:05.690 --> 14:07.470
Just perfect.

14:07.470 --> 14:12.480
I'll just do one more job before standing back
and watching how things go quietly.

14:13.790 --> 14:15.790
It's almost lunch.

14:16.400 --> 14:18.300
My stomach's so empty.

14:18.720 --> 14:20.300
U-Um...

14:20.860 --> 14:23.030
It's almost lunch... I...

14:23.580 --> 14:25.220
Stomach?

14:25.220 --> 14:27.180
Err...

14:27.540 --> 14:30.180
My stomach's so empty.

14:30.180 --> 14:30.930
My stomach...

14:31.630 --> 14:32.680
Hurts!

14:33.070 --> 14:35.370
So empty.

14:37.230 --> 14:39.600
I knew it actually!

14:39.600 --> 14:39.940
Ah...

14:41.060 --> 14:43.070
I knew it! Yeah!

14:44.260 --> 14:45.570
But, Masato...

14:45.570 --> 14:49.080
You've learned so quick
in just two weeks.

14:51.390 --> 14:54.610
I wonder when he'll go back now.

14:56.070 --> 14:59.600
Sis Miharu, that's all you've
been saying since yesterday.

14:59.600 --> 15:02.510
Huh? Really?

15:02.990 --> 15:06.430
How long do we have
to keep living like this?

15:06.810 --> 15:08.490
Like this?

15:08.490 --> 15:11.070
I should've started a new term,

15:11.070 --> 15:14.080
and a new school life as well.

15:14.620 --> 15:17.440
But my brother and Satsuki are gone,

15:18.230 --> 15:21.580
and I might not be able
to see Mom again...

15:25.440 --> 15:27.680
You must be anxious...

15:27.680 --> 15:30.180
Aren't you, Sis?

15:30.700 --> 15:32.870
I think I may be,

15:33.280 --> 15:35.690
but I have you and Masato.

15:35.690 --> 15:37.750
There's also Aishia, Celia,

15:37.750 --> 15:39.860
and Haruto as well.

15:39.860 --> 15:42.460
So I guess they can
keep me calm somehow.

15:44.740 --> 15:47.800
Don't you want to go home?

15:48.320 --> 15:50.970
There's no use rushing.

15:51.630 --> 15:54.310
Haruto's working his best for our sake,

15:54.310 --> 15:57.440
so all we can do is wait for him.

15:58.310 --> 15:59.590
Haruto...

16:00.710 --> 16:02.270
Say...

16:02.650 --> 16:05.370
What do you think of him?

16:05.370 --> 16:06.280
Huh?

16:06.280 --> 16:08.130
What, you ask?

16:08.130 --> 16:11.780
You're not supposed to be good with guys,

16:12.420 --> 16:16.830
but you act so naturally with him
as if you're having fun.

16:17.380 --> 16:19.330
I-I wonder...

16:19.930 --> 16:23.830
He's so dependable, and also so kind...

16:23.830 --> 16:24.840
Also...

16:25.220 --> 16:26.090
Also?

16:26.560 --> 16:30.590
It's because he has
the same name as Haru, I guess.

16:30.910 --> 16:32.300
So somehow...

16:32.300 --> 16:34.890
You still think about that guy?!

16:35.890 --> 16:37.370
Aki?

16:37.370 --> 16:39.390
Don't lump them together!

16:41.590 --> 16:43.360
You're being rude toward Haruto!

16:43.700 --> 16:44.320
Uh...

16:44.890 --> 16:47.780
Sorry... I didn't mean to.

16:49.150 --> 16:50.070
My bad...

16:50.570 --> 16:53.280
I'm sorry too.

16:53.820 --> 16:56.740
I'll go cool off my head.

16:56.740 --> 16:57.970
Aki...

17:00.790 --> 17:02.880
I'm such an idiot...

17:03.650 --> 17:06.130
She's not at fault, though...

17:08.330 --> 17:11.600
So she still likes that guy, huh...

17:11.600 --> 17:14.370
That Haruto Amakawa.

17:15.260 --> 17:16.540
But...

17:16.540 --> 17:17.770
Ah, geez!

17:23.970 --> 17:25.090
Aki.

17:26.550 --> 17:28.190
Sis Miharu...

17:29.540 --> 17:31.380
U-Um...

17:36.620 --> 17:38.320
Wh-Who's that?

17:38.320 --> 17:40.120
Quick, get inside!

17:47.130 --> 17:48.010
Aki!

17:58.710 --> 18:00.310
Wh-What's going on?

18:01.110 --> 18:03.290
Did something just explode?

18:03.290 --> 18:05.270
Masato, you stay here.

18:05.270 --> 18:07.320
Huh? What?

18:07.900 --> 18:09.190
Don't move!

18:10.250 --> 18:11.260
Okay?

18:16.480 --> 18:19.310
Aishia, what is that?

18:19.310 --> 18:20.620
I think they're monsters.

18:21.340 --> 18:24.370
They may be drawn to the barrier's magic.

18:24.820 --> 18:27.180
It's still alive...

18:27.180 --> 18:28.550
Both of you, stay back.

18:29.140 --> 18:31.880
Aishia, I'm leaving everyone to you.

18:32.270 --> 18:33.880
I'll protect them!

18:41.620 --> 18:44.810
Aishia! Leave those two to me!

19:01.570 --> 19:03.460
Sorry I'm late.

19:03.890 --> 19:05.100
Rio!

19:05.830 --> 19:07.210
Haruto...

19:08.980 --> 19:11.110
What was that reaction just now?

19:11.820 --> 19:12.460
So hard...

19:13.070 --> 19:15.650
Aishia, do you know what they are?

19:16.080 --> 19:19.470
I don't know, but they feel
like magical monsters.

19:20.060 --> 19:22.970
Also, I think the black one's stronger.

19:23.520 --> 19:25.790
I'll deal with the black one.

19:26.300 --> 19:29.230
Can I leave the grey ones to you?

19:38.800 --> 19:41.660
It's so fast, but too straightforward.

19:42.810 --> 19:44.450
It also attacks in large swings...

19:46.870 --> 19:48.210
What a tough creature.

19:48.590 --> 19:50.170
Can it speak?

19:51.800 --> 19:53.030
No use, huh?

19:57.690 --> 19:59.550
What life force...

20:04.720 --> 20:05.840
Huh?

20:10.660 --> 20:11.730
So...

20:12.070 --> 20:13.210
It really was a monster...

20:14.290 --> 20:16.150
I've got the other two.

20:16.800 --> 20:17.890
Thanks.

20:20.430 --> 20:22.610
Thank you, Master.

20:22.610 --> 20:24.750
That's my line.

20:25.370 --> 20:27.340
That final lip movement...

20:27.840 --> 20:29.250
As if it was saying...

20:29.580 --> 20:32.130
Kill me...

20:35.590 --> 20:38.510
I'm really sorry!

20:39.060 --> 20:41.870
It's all because I went outside!

20:41.870 --> 20:44.980
No, it's all my fault!

20:44.980 --> 20:47.260
I said something insensitive to Aki...

20:47.260 --> 20:49.470
No, I...

20:49.850 --> 20:52.210
I'm sorry, Sis Miharu.

20:52.210 --> 20:53.520
Please...

20:55.790 --> 20:57.690
I smell something nice there.

20:57.690 --> 20:59.280
Huh? Oh...

20:59.760 --> 21:03.150
Oh, right, I was preparing for lunch.

21:03.150 --> 21:06.220
Are you making omurice, by chance?

21:06.220 --> 21:08.290
Huh? Oh, yes.

21:08.700 --> 21:11.840
My stomach's so empty!
Let's have lunch!

21:11.840 --> 21:14.020
Me too!

21:14.020 --> 21:16.750
Masato, well done!

21:18.160 --> 21:19.840
I'm also hungry.

21:20.450 --> 21:22.830
Okay, I'll go prepare it right away.

21:22.830 --> 21:24.720
Aki, help me out.

21:24.720 --> 21:25.850
Yeah.

21:27.010 --> 21:28.350
Oh, right.

21:31.030 --> 21:32.890
You'll be having a new home.

21:39.870 --> 21:42.860
A group didn't return to me.

21:42.860 --> 21:44.450
Did they get lost?

21:44.890 --> 21:50.960
It's no easy feat to take down
a pack of enhanced revenants.

21:51.420 --> 21:54.630
My plan will have to be
extended of its deadline,

21:54.630 --> 21:56.460
and since I have less soldiers now,

21:56.460 --> 21:57.960
for now...

21:57.960 --> 22:02.260
I'll just convert the substrates
I have at hand here.

22:02.260 --> 22:04.050
Well, well...

22:04.050 --> 22:07.650
How many will remain now?

